{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the 28 October sprint report. The head is daaf789da794d8b7621a88d4a96a2ee7a4869316, one commit over Main 06e4d33f, for request bb928cb4, under planner promise 29b2ff7e. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, for four statements in the text. The structure, the tables and the checks are sound.\n\nI read the report at the head in full first. Then I read the first-parent history of 06e4d33f for the window, the cited decisions and requests, the day's surveys and rollout reports, and the implementation notes for the figures.\n\nA label note: the review request's text calls ca378c78 the report and eebbd53e the directory. It is the other way round. eebbd53e is notes/reports/2026-10-28-sprint-report.md, and ca378c78 is `notes`. The request body names eebbd53e, which is correct.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Base and delta. One commit, daaf789d, whose parent is 06e4d33f. It adds one file of 317 lines, and the worktree is clean.\n- Landings. The first-parent history from 17:00 on 27 October to 17:00 on 28 October has ten landings. Each one's time, path count and, where given, commit count matches the report. The counts are from the merge's first parent to the merge.\n- Deployments. All 25 rows match the deploy receipts and surveys: the 19:31 round in rollout report c676a6c7, the 21:31 round in 4cba81d4 and bc4a5111, dap-hostnone bb279a3b in 4cba81d4, and the later rounds in c41c157a, c940cf34, 5a1ba9ca, 2671535c, 8ee33a0b and 33a65115. There are eight rounds of the three room Workers, and each row has the Main it was deployed from.\n- Census. Grow had 11 of 11 verified, lending 8 of 8, and demo 6 verified and 5 unavailable, as in c676a6c7.\n- First room with host `none` (4cba81d4). Register 21, Directory 20, Destination 16, Membership 8, Rules 10 and Inbox 1 match the G1 note. `verify --all` found all 6 scopes consistent. The refusals were `no-repository` and `host-unknown`.\n- Other figures:\n  - The CLI witness made 1,000 entry reads and 0 new session requests.\n  - The J3 manifest is 321,021 bytes against the 40,960-byte advisory.\n  - J3 adds five new modules in packages/checkers/src, plus the Node entry, the relay and the Dockerfile.\n  - The tmpfs size options support \"disk limits\".\n  - The local-network ranges and the MCP bearer keys match the LAN keys note.\n  - The second spike's six patterns and pinned digests match 4694a0ce. The canonical-spelling counts match 2ad35350.\n- Decisions and filings:\n  - Each cited act exists and says what the report says: 3240b82d, 999ffe93, 209d11d0, 9a20093b, 3ce7ade0, ed818781, f73805e4, a3af9cf9, 60a1eb82, 8d212c9a, d8b5d72b and d81e308a.\n  - DX-B2 3770c687 is not in the Filed table, which is correct: 11150ee2 retired it into DX-T4 d49269fd.\n- Documents:\n  - check-doc-links on an export of the head: 731 links, 0 broken.\n  - check-notes 06e4d33f daaf789d: 0 warnings.\n  - check-commit-messages: 1 checked, 0 flagged.\n  - `git diff --check`: clean.\n  - No line is over 79 characters, table rows included.\n- Wording:\n  - The only products named are GitHub and Cloudflare's parts (Artifacts, Durable Object, Workers).\n  - The container runtime is called \"the Linux guest\".\n  - There are no comparisons and no reference to anyone's instructions.\n\n## Changes requested\n\n1. J3 cost-of-change entry, lines 225 to 228. The first review point is inverted. Today an empty run directory, left by a crash after `mkdir` and before claim.json, already leaves the job waiting forever, because `find` throws. The fix is that such a directory, once older than the grace period, should end as `run-lost`. The entry says it \"should leave a job waiting\", which is the defect itself. The planner's 15:32 survey had it right: \"empty run directory leaves a job waiting\". The same sentence also says \"the four non-blocking review points\" but lists three. Either list the manifest size as the fourth, or say \"the three other points\". A suggested form: \"an empty run directory should end as run-lost instead of leaving the job waiting, the claim-size refusal needs its own name, and a failing step that writes to stderr should end as failed, not run-lost\".\n2. Test Worker count, lines 13 and 14. \"A test Worker was deployed twice\" does not match the evidence. dap-hostnone had three versions: 04ec1540 (no pin), e99eb608 (the redeploy after the failed pin patch, as correction 0a953799 records) and bb279a3b (REGISTER_SCOPE set). Say \"three times\", or name the final version only.\n3. Retirement wait, lines 198 and 199. \"Waited four and a half hours between approval and landing\" is not the measured interval. Approval 0f2c9cff was filed at 00:43 and the merge was at 06:02, which is 5 h 19 min. Four and a half hours is the interval from the placement decision 209d11d0 (01:31) to the landing. Say which one you mean, and compute it.\n4. Census wording, lines 57 and 58, and the note under the deploy table. \"The expected state for rooms whose founders have left\" is not in the evidence. Rollout report c676a6c7 says the five rows are refused `forbidden` because the demo operator key did not found those scopes. The evidence does not say whether the founders left. Say \"rooms the operator did not found\", or similar.\n\nNot blocking: \"nine name mistakes … are compile errors\" comes from the first spike (99c4756a), not the second. The paragraph speaks of both spikes, so a reader may take it as the second's. \"Of the first spike\" after the figure would place it.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe structure suits a reader who might adopt the work:\n- stories for the user-visible changes;\n- the landings, deploys and filings in tables or lists, with IDs;\n- the cost-of-change review with eight entries, each giving the cost, the alternative and whether to revisit;\n- the decisions, then what is in progress, what did not happen, and the commitments.\n\nThe Status line matches main once this lands. Once the four statements are corrected, the report is a stable projection of the window.\n\n## Security\n\nThe report adds documents only, and no code, configuration or evidence path changes. It names no secret, token value or custody path. The security statements in the J3 story match the verdict: no network, read-only root, no capabilities, custody on the host, and a refused result for another tree. The local-network statement matches the LAN keys note.\n\n## Simplification\n\nOne file of 317 lines covers ten landings, eight deploy rounds and the day's filings. That is in proportion. The figures appear once each, so the four corrections are local edits.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved, subject to the corrections.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- Request conditions:\n  - met: the ten landings with times and path counts; the deploy table against the surveys; the wording rules; prose lines; check-doc-links; check-notes; no reference to anyone's instructions;\n  - not met: \"each figure traces to a landing note, a verdict or a survey assert\", at items 1 to 4 above.\n\nA head with these corrections needs only the changed lines checked again.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eebbd53e7cd304264313d8aa4f43a0d45d5e9ad4","binding":"assigned","head":"daaf789da794d8b7621a88d4a96a2ee7a4869316","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8be110069622280a9d8e74799a31cbe5363a9375\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:29b2ff7ef0233e525de3e0bd1e0aa22cc7c56a55\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8be110069622280a9d8e74799a31cbe5363a9375","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}